   174	def validate_readings(readings):
   175	    """Refuses readings that are not exactly what `mark_cards.readings` writes, before any verdict or diagnostic (one owner for the
   176	    readings' shape). The whole file is walked top down, and every container's type is checked before it is read:
   177	    - the top level holds matters, mapping, distinct, cards, controls and inputs, and may hold matter_first_day;
   178	    - mapping, cards and distinct each hold the six draws;
   179	    - a matter is {matter: text, company_figure: a JSON boolean};
   180	    - a card holds worth, answer, type, guardrail and covering, and may hold opened. A mark is a frozen mark or a split of two different
   181	      ones; an answer may be "no answer"; the guardrail is a JSON boolean; covering is a JSON boolean or "split"; opened is null or a day;
   182	    - a mapped matter is on the matter list, with a non-empty list of {question: a carded question of the draw, covers: true or "split"};
   183	    - a draw's distinct counts are ids, duplicates_both and duplicates_split: non-negative integers, the duplicates no more than the ids;
   184	    - matter_first_day maps listed matters to days; a day is YYYY-MM-DD;
   185	    - the controls are lists: plants and supported of answer marks, repeats_same of JSON booleans;
   186	    - the inputs are the seven named paths and fingerprints, as text."""
